uld  not confirm whether that happened  whether that meeting between the cio  director and the new  um  head of the taliban actually happened  but um a press conference that covered a  whole range of issues um quickfire  questions from  the world's media that are here in kabul  i'll just read you through some of the  other comments that were made  as you said he said that  there's been no agreement made on the  extension of the deadline for the  evacuation that ongoing evacuation at  the airport  with mounting pressure on the u.s  administration  to put in for a bid on that on an  extension of that evacuation um the  taliban spokesperson said that uh the  media had started working he said that  uh every day the freedom of the media in  this country improves obviously a lot of  fear amongst media workers local media  workers  that many of whom have fled the country  already many of whom are at the airport  getting onto flights now  but he there the taliban spokesman  trying to allay those fears  he also said that um the crowd at the  airport can go home we guarantee their  security well the taliban have already  said that um  although they will not agree to any  extension of this deadline they say that  people who want to leave the country can  leave the country eventually if they  have the right paperwork  the right visas and they can get onto  commercial flights but of course nobody  knows when commercial flights will  restart  there was also a comment about the issue  of the panshir valley now the panchayat  valley as we've been reporting around  100 kilometers from here um there is  it's the last pocket of resistance if  you like  against the taliban  we know that the taliban have surrounded  the area or that's what they are  reporting  the group inside there in staunch  opposition to the taliban saying they  want guarantees that any uh new  government would be fully inclusive of  all ethnicities  and would be open and fair well  they have said that if that does 